 could also be viewed as $y=cos⁡(-x).$" 13194139533680 true] [17592186060305 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533680 true] [17592186060305 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/c27ff316601ece28946ef45711690d6aabca92a4c35f07b0b1cc1c0982fb5d8e.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-cos⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, translate it by $1$ unit **up** to give $y=-cos⁡x+1$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-cos⁡x+1.$" 13194139533680 true] [17592186246298 1017 #edb/ref 17592186246299 13194139533680 true] [17592186246298 1089 "q-118348" 13194139533680 true] [17592186246298 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533680 true] [17592186246298 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/f2d3945780d6d042ae5fa01905cf7740fca0f5f80307124556a1b4724f691683.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the graph shown above?" 13194139533680 true] [17592186246298 1113 #uuid "2e7f3919-6ad5-5ead-b766-27f8f2a6a127" 13194139533680 true] [17592186246298 1138 false 13194139533680 true] [17592186246298 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/6ba976f250811d1ba3109f4aecbfdb2a4de4ee86300fa867e80e2087aa21601f.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-sin⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $\\frac{7}{4}$ to give $y=-\\frac{7}{4}sin⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-\\frac{7}{4}sin⁡x.$" 13194139533680 true] [17592186246299 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246300 13194139533680 true] [17592186246299 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246301 13194139533680 true] [17592186246299 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246302 13194139533680 true] [17592186246299 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246303 13194139533680 tru